<title>FRANCE: Colas 1996 net attrib rises.</title>
<headline>Colas 1996 net attrib rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     400  vs	     390</p>
<p>    Net						408  vs	     404</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)			 25  vs	    same</p>
<p>    Cashflow				     1,053  vs	   1,065</p>
<p>    Sales					 19,354  vs	  19,240</p>
<p>NOTE - Road builder and civil engineering group Colas said in a results statement that consolidated sales for this year should be around 25 billion francs. It expected decline in the French roads building market to be less marked than in 1996 unless there was a spending freeze.</p>
<p>Abroad, the outlook was generally favourable because of the more favourable context in North America and Asia.</p>
<p>It said &quot;external growth developments&quot; would continue after the purchase of 50 percent of Finnish Valtatie Oy and purchase of SWTD in Britain.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
